<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Traprain Law Treasure</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 5th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/traprain-law">Traprain Law</a> Treasure is a hoard of late Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>, more than 250 pieces of cut and crushed tableware weighing over 20 kg, found in 1919 on the hillfort of Traprain Law in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-lothian">East Lothian</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. Buried in the early 5th century, it was probably a payment or gift to the leaders of the Votadini, and it is now in the National Museum of Scotland.</p></div>
